  "description": "#6755 — a tag's `tag_properties`: a list of keys a user can set (a built-in is refused), offered on the blocks directly tagged with the tag or with one its name nests under, minus the keys a block holds (`list_suggested_properties`); `set_property_on_tagged_blocks` sets a value on the tag's blocks (nested tags included, held values overwritten) as one `set_property` per block, refused when the acknowledged counts are stale (`UnacknowledgedPropertyLoss`), leaving the Trash be, and one `undo_ops` of its ops puts every block back. Seed: page S1 holds S2 tagged `book` (S5), S3 tagged `book` holding `stage` = draft after O6, S4 tagged `book/novel` (S6), and S7 tagged `book`, trashed by O5. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
